@startuml Task Orchestrator Workflow

!theme plain
title τ²-Bench Task Management and Orchestration Workflow

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam component {
    BackgroundColor lightblue
    BorderColor black
}

package "Data Layer" {
    [tasks.json] as TaskJSON
    [db.json] as DatabaseJSON
    [policy.md] as PolicyMD
    note right of TaskJSON : Contains task definitions\nwith user scenarios and\nevaluation criteria
}

package "Configuration & Registry" {
    component [Registry] as Registry
    component [CLI Parser] as CLI
    component [RunConfig] as RunConfig
    note right of Registry
**Registry manages:**
- Available domains (airline, retail, telecom, mock)
- Agent implementations and constructors
- User implementations and constructors
- Task loaders per domain

**Key Methods:**
• get_info() → RegistryInfo
• get_env_constructor(domain) → Environment class
• get_agent_constructor(agent) → Agent class
• get_user_constructor(user) → User class
• get_tasks_loader(task_set) → Task loading function
end note
}

package "Task Loading" {
    component [Domain Environment] as DomainEnv
    component [Task Loader] as TaskLoader
    component [Task Model] as TaskModel
    note right of TaskLoader : Domain-specific task loaders\n(get_tasks functions)
}

package "Orchestration Core" {
    component [Orchestrator] as Orchestrator
    component [BaseAgent/LLMAgent] as Agent
    component [BaseUser/UserSimulator] as User
    component [Environment] as Environment
    component [SimulationRun] as SimulationRun

    package "Message Types" {
        component [AssistantMessage] as AssistantMsg
        component [UserMessage] as UserMsg
        component [ToolMessage] as ToolMsg
        component [MultiToolMessage] as MultiToolMsg
        component [ToolCall] as ToolCall
    }
}

package "Execution Engine" {
    component [run_tasks] as RunTasks
    component [run_task] as RunTask
    component [ThreadPoolExecutor] as ThreadPool
}

package "Evaluation & Results" {
    component [Evaluator] as Evaluator
    component [Metrics Calculator] as Metrics
    component [Results Storage] as Results
}

' Data flow connections
CLI --> RunConfig : parses arguments
RunConfig --> Registry : queries available options
Registry --> TaskLoader : gets task loader for domain
TaskLoader --> TaskJSON : reads tasks.json
TaskJSON --> TaskModel : deserializes to Task objects

Registry --> DomainEnv : gets environment constructor
DomainEnv --> DatabaseJSON : loads domain database
DomainEnv --> PolicyMD : loads domain policy

RunTasks --> TaskModel : receives list of Task objects
RunTasks --> ThreadPool : manages concurrent execution
ThreadPool --> RunTask : executes individual task/trial

RunTask --> Agent : creates agent instance
RunTask --> User : creates user simulator
RunTask --> Environment : creates environment
RunTask --> Orchestrator : creates orchestrator

Orchestrator --> Agent : get_init_state_info()
Orchestrator --> User : get_init_state_info()
Orchestrator --> Environment : set_state()

Orchestrator --> SimulationRun : creates simulation result

note as OrchestrationDetails
**Orchestration.step() - Message Flow State Machine**

**AGENT/ENV → USER Flow:**
• Orchestrator.generate_next_message(message, user_state)
• Input: AssistantMessage | ToolMessage | MultiToolMessage
• Returns: (UserMessage, UserState)
• user_msg.validate() + UserSimulator.is_stop() check
• trajectory.append(user_msg)
• Route: user_msg.is_tool_call() ? ENV : AGENT

**USER/ENV → AGENT Flow:**
• Orchestrator.generate_next_message(message, agent_state)
• Input: UserMessage | ToolMessage | MultiToolMessage
• Returns: (AssistantMessage, AgentState)
• agent_msg.validate() + agent.is_stop() check
• trajectory.append(agent_msg)
• Route: agent_msg.is_tool_call() ? ENV : USER

**AGENT/USER → ENV Flow:**
• message.is_tool_call() check required
• For each tool_call in message.tool_calls:
  - Environment.get_response(tool_call)
  - Environment.make_tool_call() + sync_tools()
  - Returns: ToolMessage(content, error, requestor)
• trajectory.extend(tool_msgs)
• If multiple: create MultiToolMessage

**Termination Conditions:**
• UserSimulator.is_stop() → USER_STOP
• agent.is_stop() → AGENT_STOP
• step_count >= max_steps → MAX_STEPS
• num_errors >= max_errors → TOO_MANY_ERRORS
end note

OrchestrationDetails .. Orchestrator

RunTask --> Evaluator : evaluate_simulation()
Evaluator --> SimulationRun : adds reward_info

RunTasks --> Metrics : compute_metrics()
RunTasks --> Results : stores final results

note right of Agent
**Agent Classes:**
• BaseAgent - Abstract interface
• LLMAgent - Standard conversational agent
• LLMGTAgent - Agent with ground truth actions
• LLMSoloAgent - Agent with user + assistant tools

**Key Methods:**
• generate_next_message(message, state)
  → (AssistantMessage, AgentState)
• get_init_state(message_history?) → AgentState
• is_stop(message) → bool
• set_seed(seed) - For reproducibility
end note

note right of User
**User Classes:**
• BaseUser - Abstract interface
• UserSimulator - LLM-based user simulation
• DummyUser - No-op user for solo mode

**Key Methods:**
• generate_next_message(message, state)
  → (UserMessage, UserState)
• get_init_state(message_history?) → UserState
• is_stop(message) → bool (checks "###STOP###")
end note

' Notes about the workflow
note top of Orchestrator
**Orchestration State Machine:**
• from_role: Role.AGENT | Role.USER | Role.ENV
• to_role: Role.AGENT | Role.USER | Role.ENV
• message: Current message being processed
• trajectory: Full conversation history

**Key Methods:**
• Orchestrator.initialize() - Setup states
• Orchestrator.step() - Process one message
• Orchestrator.run() - Main simulation loop
• Orchestrator.get_trajectory() - Final results
end note

note bottom of TaskModel
**Task Structure (Task class):**
- id: unique identifier
- user_scenario: StructuredUserInstructions
- evaluation_criteria: EvaluationCriteria
- initial_state: InitialState (optional)

**EvaluationCriteria contains:**
- actions: List[Action] - Expected actions
- env_assertions: List[EnvAssertion] - Environment checks
- nl_assertions: List[str] - Natural language checks
- reward_basis: List[RewardType] - Scoring criteria
end note

note left of Environment
**Environment provides:**
- Domain-specific tools via ToolKitBase
- Database operations via DB class
- Policy enforcement
- Tool response handling

**Key Methods:**
• get_response(tool_call) → ToolMessage
• make_tool_call(name, requestor, **args)
• sync_tools() - Update tool availability
• get_tools() - Return available tools
end note

@enduml
